<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine monthly oilseed crushings.</title>
<headline>Argentine monthly oilseed crushings.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine mills crushed 1,523,763 tonnes of oilseed in October 1996 against 1,390,836 tonnes in October 1995, the Agriculture Secretariat said.</p>
<p>(Breakdown in tonnes, year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> Soybean	     1,095,061    (954,752)</p>
<p> Sunflowerseed	 415,137    (423,397)</p>
<p> Linseed		   1,648	(6,178)</p>
<p> Groundnutseed	  11,917	(6,535)</p>
<p> Cottonseed		  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p>Output in October was as follows:</p>
<p> ..............Oils...................Meals</p>
<p> Soybean     194,326    (169,416)    875,083     (781,257)</p>
<p> Sunflower   171,307    (167,706)    173,263     (178,855)</p>
<p> Linseed	   434	(2,368)	  nil	   (nil)</p>
<p> Groundnut     4,588	(2,406)	6,793	 (3,757)</p>
<p> Cottonseed	nil	  (nil)	  nil	   (nil)</p>
<p> .......................Expellers</p>
<p> Soybean    2,428   (3,120)  Groundnut   nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Sunflower    nil     (nil)  Cottonseed  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Linseed    1,186   (4,679)</p>
<p>Crushings from January to October, with the same period in</p>
<p>1995 in brackets, were:</p>
<p> Soybean	     8,586,595    (7,277,196)</p>
<p> Sunflowerseed     4,416,097    (4,283,576)</p>
<p> Linseed		 119,571	(108,487)</p>
<p> Groundnutseed	 107,216	 (96,139)</p>
<p> Cottonseed	    432,947	(419,616)</p>
<p>Output in January through October (1995 in brackets):</p>
<p> ..............Oils...................Meals</p>
<p> Soybean   1,523,574  (1,252,684)  6,872,092  (5,760,189)</p>
<p>Sunflower 1,775,129  (1,715,113)  1,859,777  (1,832,567)  Linseed	38,705     (35,893)	  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Groundnut    41,533     (37,358)     61,632     (54,100)</p>
<p> Cottonseed   66,659     (64,902)    205,507    (194,791)</p>
<p> .......................Expellers</p>
<p> Soybean    28,654 (46,886)   Groundnut   nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Sunflower   6,419  (4,234)   Cottonseed  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Linseed    78,866 (72,306)</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541-318-0655</p>
